# oracle-capture-signin-page-links.rb - the pinned Ruby's own bytes for the
# SIGNED-OUT SIGN-IN PAGE'S TWO LINKS (registry row cap-S4, "Sign-in link to
# sign up, and link to reset password").
#
# The row's contract: the signed-out sign-in page links to sign up and to
# reset the password. Seven pinned files own the two links and the bytes
# around them:
#
#   1. card-mod-account-0.20.0/set/self/signin.rb - THE TWO LINKS:
#      `signup_link` is `link_to_card :signup, t(:account_or_sign_up), path:
#      { action: :new, mark: :signup }` and `reset_password_link` is
#      `link_to_view :edit, t(:account_reset_password), path: { slot: { hide:
#      :board_link } }`; `signin_button` is the third control in the block.
#   2. card-mod-account-0.20.0/set/self/signin/core.haml - THE BLOCK: the
#      `.form-group.signin-buttons` division holds `.reset-password-link`,
#      `.signin-button` and `.signup-button`, in that order.
#   3. card-mod-account-0.20.0/config/locales/en.yml - THE THREE TEXTS:
#      account_or_sign_up is "...or sign up!", account_reset_password is
#      "Reset password" and account_sign_in is "Sign in".
#   4. card-mod-format-0.20.0/set/all/links.rb - THE ANCHOR SHAPES:
#      `link_to` puts the path LAST into the href, `link_to_card` adds the
#      known/wanted class, `link_to_view` is a remote link with
#      `rel: "nofollow"` and the "slotter" class.
#   5. card-mod-format-0.20.0/lib/card/path.rb - THE TWO DESTINATIONS:
#      `new_cardtype` renders "new/<mark>" and `base` renders "<mark>/<view>".
#   6. card-mod-format-0.20.0/lib/card/path/cast_params.rb - THE SLOT HIDE
#      SERIALIZATION: a scalar slot hide is wrapped by `Array.wrap`, which is
#      why the key carries the `[]` suffix.
#
# The capture reads the pinned gemset and writes nothing but its own JSON
# fixture. It does NOT boot the oracle deck.
#
# Run (from the repository root, with the pinned gemset on the gem path):
#   GEM_PATH="reference-harness/ruby-oracle-gems/ruby/3.4.0:$(ruby -e 'print Gem.default_dir')" \
#     ruby tests/card/mod-loader/oracle-capture-signin-page-links.rb
#
# Determinism contract: the output JSON is pretty-printed with deeply sorted
# keys and a trailing newline, and carries NO timestamp, so a re-run is
# byte-stable against what is committed.

